## Modules

| Module | Cryptographic primitives | Category |
|---|---|---|
| [SAILOR core](#sailor-lightweight-risc-v-cryptography-core) | AES, SHA-256/-512 (RISC-V *Zkn*), constant-time execution (*Zkt*) | Conventional |
| [Ascon engine](#ascon-engine) | Ascon-AEAD, Ascon-Hash, Ascon-XOF | Lightweight |
| [Unified SHA-3/SHAKE engine](#unified-sha-3shake-engine) | SHA3-224/-256/-384/-512, SHAKE128/256 | Conventional |
| [Rocket core](#rocket-core) | – (general-purpose RV32IM processing) | Processing core |

### SAILOR: Lightweight RISC-V Cryptography Core

SAILOR is a family of lightweight and energy-efficient RISC-V cores that serves as the HW-RoT controller.

- RV32I base instruction set with a three-stage pipeline
- Serializable datapath with configurable widths of 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, or 32 bits
- Independently selectable RISC-V scalar cryptography extensions:

  | Extension | Description |
  |---|---|
  | Zbkb | Bit-manipulation for cryptography |
  | Zbkc | Carry-less multiplication |
  | Zbkx | Crossbar permutations |
  | Zkne & Zknd | AES encryption & decryption |
  | Zknh | SHA-256 & SHA-512 |
  | **Zkn** | NIST algorithm suite (Zbkb, Zbkc, Zbkx, Zkne, Zknd, Zknh) |
  | **Zkt** | Data-independent execution latency |

- Resource sharing with existing functional units, e.g., a compact combined AES encryption/decryption
  S-box and ALU reuse for SHA-2 bit-permutations

### Ascon Engine

A compact single engine for the NIST lightweight cryptography standard Ascon.

- Supports authenticated encryption with associated data (AEAD), hashing, and extendable-output
  function (XOF) modes in one engine
- Round-based implementation with a single 320-bit state register
- Finite-state machine reduced to two states (non-message and message state) shared across all modes
- Optimized state initialization and low-complexity padding offset computation

### Unified SHA-3/SHAKE Engine

A unified engine for the SHA-3 hash functions and the SHAKE extendable-output functions, complementing
the SHA-2 support of SAILOR.

- Runtime selection of SHA3-224/-256/-384/-512 and SHAKE128/256
- Round-based implementation with a single Keccak permutation core
- Byte-partitioned state register for flexible, mode-specific rate and capacity configuration

### Rocket Core

The [Rocket core](https://github.com/chipsalliance/rocket-chip) is a 5-stage, in-order RISC-V core,
deployed in its 32-bit RV32IM configuration.

